//@ run-pass
//@ exit-code: 240
// CAPACITY BOUNDARY WITNESS: 3000 live functions in one merged IrModule.
//
// Over the old IR_MAX_FUNCS = 2048 and under the new 4096. It exists because
// raising that constant alone was NOT enough and the failure was silent.
//
// Two bounds guards in the backend read the literal 2048 while the arrays they
// guarded grew with the constant:
//
//     native/elf.sio:125                  if fn_idx >= 0 && fn_idx < 2048
//     native/codegen_x86_linux.sio:5800   if fn_index >= 0 && fn_index < 2048
//
// Past the literal, a function's symbol name and its code offset were simply
// DROPPED. Measured by bisect against a compiler with IR_MAX_FUNCS = 4096 and
// those literals still in place: correct up to 2045 functions, and from exactly
// 2046 the produced binary EXITS 0 AND PRINTS NOTHING. No error from the
// compiler, no signal from the program. Raising the IR constant without these
// two lines converts an honest "too many functions" refusal into a wrong
// answer, which is strictly worse than the wall it removes.
//
// ir_cap_0() returns 3001, and 3001 % 251 == 240.
use ir_capacity_mod::{wrap, W, ir_cap_0}

fn main() -> i64 with Mut, Panic, Div {
    let w = wrap::<i64>(ir_cap_0())
    return w.val % 251
}
